  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-7-PPR-4000006738</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-7" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Netherlands</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Digital for Development Hub (D4D-Hub): enabling Dutch digital development priorities through EU coordination and collaboration.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The action&apos;s primary focus is the coordination of efforts in the field of digitalisation for development (D4D) through European collaboration. This will contribute to increased impact of D4D efforts, particularly in the fields of the Twin Transition (Climate + Digital), Digital Innovation, the Digital Economy and the development of local digital ecosystems. Specific attention will be given to the position and empowerment of women. While coordination efforts (and subsequent activities) will have impact in the focus countries for Dutch development cooperation, the action will be implemented by the Netherlands Enterprise Agency (NEA/Rijksdienst voor Ondernemend Nederland, RVO), through its office in The Hague. The total budget is including EUR 387,298 implementation costs (uitvoeringskosten RVO).</narrative>
  </description>
